.TH QUADRF-NEARFIELD 1 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-nearfield \- coherent 4x4 MIMO near-field phasor display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-nearfield
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cycles the four transmit antennas in time-division multiplex, digitally
down-converts the CSI ring buffer against a 1 MHz DDS tone, and draws one
phasor pane per receive channel. Each pane shows the three bistatic paths
from the other transmitters; the monostatic path (same TX and RX index) is
blanked. On start the app enables 4-channel RX interleave, analog TX, and a
5800 MHz LO. Display scale is fixed (pixels per unit I/Q); Up/Down zoom the
plot only.
.SH KEYS
The SDL window must have keyboard focus (click it).
.TP
.B Space
Latch the current bistatic phasors as a calibration offset (direct-path
zero).
.TP
.BR Up ", " +
Increase the display scale by 1.2.
.TP
.BR Down ", " \-
Decrease the display scale by 1.2.
.TP
.B Escape
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-psd (1),
.BR quadrf-rf-vision (1),
.BR quadrf-jtag (1)
